[{"id":126291,"sender_id":612,"sender_full_name":"nLab edit announcer","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/c58b62e30f75d369349d5c08eee8f6b9?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/2-Latest-Changes/topic/well-founded.20relation.20.282.29/near/126291\">#64</a> Provide an equivalent phrasing of the <strong><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo>≺</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\prec</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.5782em;vertical-align:-0.0391em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">≺</span></span></span></span>-inductive subset</strong> condition that might be slightly more intuitive to students/novices.</p>\n<p>At least for me, I spent a little time mentally untangling the quantifiers until I realized the subset of A was just the left partial application to <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo>≺</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\prec</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.5782em;vertical-align:-0.0391em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">≺</span></span></span></span>.</p>\n<p>John Ericson</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/revision/diff/well-founded+relation/38\">diff</a>, <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/revision/well-founded+relation/38\">v38</a>, <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/well-founded+relation\">current</a></p>","timestamp":1793403597,"subject":"well-founded relation (2)","stream_id":2,"display_recipient":"Latest Changes","reactions":[]},{"id":126292,"sender_id":612,"sender_full_name":"nLab edit announcer","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/c58b62e30f75d369349d5c08eee8f6b9?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/2-Latest-Changes/topic/well-founded.20relation.20.282.29/near/126292\">#65</a> Use <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mspace></mspace><mspace width=\"0.1111em\"/><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0.17em\"></mo><mtext> ⁣</mtext><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">:</mo><mspace width=\"0.3333em\"/><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x\\colon S</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span><span class=\"mspace nobreak\"></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1111em;\"></span><span class=\"mpunct\"></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:-0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mrel\">:</span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.3333em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0576em;\">S</span></span></span></span> in the set-builder notation, for consistency. We can just use set notation for the subsets (the built set without a name and <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">A</span></span></span></span>).</p>\n<p>Also I meant right partial application, not left one, in the previous edit log.</p>\n<p>John Ericson</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/revision/diff/well-founded+relation/38\">diff</a>, <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/revision/well-founded+relation/38\">v38</a>, <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/well-founded+relation\">current</a></p>","timestamp":1793404730,"subject":"well-founded relation (2)","stream_id":2,"display_recipient":"Latest Changes","reactions":[]}]